Found it. The `checkCredentials()` method checks for `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, OAuth credentials, and settings.json — but it has **no Vertex AI check**. It doesn't look at `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX` at all.

Easiest fix: add `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX` to your settings.json env block, which it does read for `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. But since it only checks for that specific key, we need to give it something it recognizes.

Add a dummy `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` to your settings so the UI auth check passes, while the actual auth still goes through Vertex:

```bash
cat > /tmp/fix.js << 'SCRIPT'
const fs = require('fs');
const p = '/home/claude/.claude/settings.json';
const s = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8'));
s.env = s.env || {};
s.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = 'vertex-auth-via-gcloud';
fs.writeFileSync(p, JSON.stringify(s, null, 2));
SCRIPT
node /tmp/fix.js
```

This sets a placeholder API key in settings.json that satisfies the UI's auth check. Claude Code itself will still use Vertex AI because `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX=1` takes priority over the API key.

Reload `http://192.168.1.121:3059/` after running that.

Let's use node instead — sed is fighting the special characters:

```bash
cat > /tmp/fix-models.js << 'SCRIPT'
const fs = require('fs');
const p = '/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@cloudcli-ai/cloudcli/dist-server/server/modules/providers/list/claude/claude-models.provider.js';
let c = fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8');
c = c.replace(/Opus 4\.8/g, 'Opus 4.6');
fs.writeFileSync(p, c);
SCRIPT
node /tmp/fix-models.js
```

Then verify and restart:

```bash
grep -E "opus|Opus" /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@cloudcli-ai/cloudcli/dist-server/server/modules/providers/list/claude/claude-models.provider.js
kill $(pgrep -f "node /usr/local/bin/cloudcli")
```

